{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-250380-r4531782","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Fattoush","sourcePageId":250380,"sourceRevision":"4531782","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-08-21T00:52:45Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Fattoush&oldid=4531782","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:53.340Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for salad","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using lettuce","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1bbd0ef0a7d196cb6e7755446e2b56afbb53f7963ad5e136304a5abc1cbe9a11","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Salad recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Fattoush''' is a Lebanese salad, good for hot weather. The recipe uses two unusual ingredients: [[Cookbook:Sumac|sumac]] and [[Cookbook:Purslane|purslane]]. Ground sumac consists of the red sumac berries, and it used in Middle Eastern, particularly Lebanese, cooking. Purslane is a succulent with a lemony flavor, and it makes a nice salad green.\n==Ingredients==\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n* ⅓ cup [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n* 2 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Sumac|sumac]] powder\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n* Ground [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]] to taste\n* 1 head [[Cookbook:Romaine Lettuce|romaine lettuce]], torn into bite-size pieces\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Cucumber|cucumber]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 2 large [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], diced\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Green Onion|green onions]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* ¼ cup chopped fresh flat-leaf [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n* ¼ cup chopped fresh [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]]\n* 1 green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], seeded and chopped\n* 1 cup chopped [[Cookbook:Purslane|purslane]]\n* ½ package (5 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) [[Cookbook:Arugula|arugula]] (rocket)\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Pita|pita]] rounds, toasted and torn into pieces\n\n==Procedure==\n#Mix the water and cornstarch in a small [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] over medium-high heat until thickened. \n#Remove from heat, and mix in lemon juice, garlic, sumac, salt, and pepper. \n#Refrigerate until ready to use.\n#In a large bowl, toss together the lettuce, cucumber, tomatoes, green onions, parsley, mint, bell pepper, purslane, and arugula. \n#Toss with the dressing, and serve with pita.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* If purslane is unavailable, [[Cookbook:Watercress|watercress]], parsley, or [[Cookbook:Arugula|arugula]] may be substituted.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for salad]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lettuce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fattoush","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-